# hyperbox — the pad row + REC (v4), on the boot panel (DRUMS is already open).
# Regression track for the tap-record: the trace's `gridn` (live step count) must GROW while
# `rec`=1 and hold still while `rec`=0. A tap onto a step that already has a hit leaves gridn
# unchanged — that's an overwrite, not a miss, so read the deltas not the count.
#   node tools/play.js hyperbox script tools/clips/hyperbox/04-pads.script --headless --frames 240 --trace t.jsonl
# frames 240
# Geometry (drums open: body y=66): lanes at 70/90/110/130, pads 152..170,
# pad x = 26/72/118/164 (w 44), REC at 210..256.
click 20 30 160       # BD pad, REC still OFF: it sounds, the grid must NOT change
click 45 76 160       # SD pad, same
click 70 232 160      # arm REC (the light blinks on the beat from here)
click 100 30 160      # BD  -> lands on the nearest step
click 120 76 160      # SD
click 140 122 160     # CH
click 160 168 160     # CP  (the sparse lane: this one is always a new step)
click 190 232 160     # disarm
click 215 168 160     # CP again, disarmed: sounds, writes nothing
